{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778975708570,"sessionID":"ses_1cccbecf5ffeX5PzJALhbXd9oH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_DcAf6xuIyzl0jAOdb6UAtkAq","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I updated `MONDO:0980992` (`Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9`) with the exact synonym `GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome` and added a sourced GINS3 gene association based on `PMID:38773883` and the existing OMIM mapping.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed issue #9933 by updating `MONDO:0980992` (`Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9`).\n+\n+Changes made:\n+\n+- Added definition: `A Meier-Gorlin syndrome that is caused by homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in the GINS3 gene.`\n+- Added exact synonym: `GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome`.\n+- Added `has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in` relationship to `http://identifiers.org/hgnc/25851` (`GINS3`).\n+- Added issue tracker metadata for `https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9933`.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+\n+- The issue discussion identified existing term `MONDO:0980992` as the appropriate disease term for GINS3-associated Meier-Gorlin syndrome.\n+- `PMID:38773883` reports additional individuals with homozygous GINS3 variants and functional yeast evidence supporting pathogenicity, consistent with adding the requested synonym and explicit gene association.\n+- `HGNC:25851` was verified as the approved identifier for human gene `GINS3` using the HGNC REST endpoint.\n+\n+Completed checklist:\n+\n+- Read imported issue title, body, and comments from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Reviewed the current `MONDO:0980992` stanza.\n+- Reviewed the parent `MONDO:0016817` (`Meier-Gorlin syndrome`) for consistency.\n+- Verified `PMID:38773883` metadata and abstract via PubMed.\n+- Verified `HGNC:25851` as `GINS3` via HGNC.\n+- Applied edits using the checkout/checkin workflow.\n+- Ran local ROBOT syntax validation: `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o mondo-edit.TMP.obo`.\n+\n+Validation note:\n+\n+- Required ODK normalization (`make NORM`) could not be run in this evaluation environment because `docker` is not installed. The local ROBOT conversion/syntax check completed successfully.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I updated `MONDO:0980992` (`Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9`) with the exact synonym `GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome` and added a sourced GINS3 gene association based on `PMID:38773883` and the existing OMIM mapping.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+Addressed issue #9933 by updating `MONDO:0980992` (`Meier-Gorlin syndrome 9`).\n+\n+Changes made:\n+\n+- Added definition: `A Meier-Gorlin syndrome that is caused by homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in the GINS3 gene.`\n+- Added exact synonym: `GINS3 Meier-Gorlin syndrome`.\n+- Added `has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in` relationship to `http://identifiers.org/hgnc/25851` (`GINS3`).\n+- Added issue tracker metadata for `https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9933`.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+\n+- The issue discussion identified existing term `MONDO:0980992` as the appropriate disease term for GINS3